# The policy set AND the required-check enforcement surface, owned by the
# repository owner (decision 0009 as amended 2026-09-16; #201 comments
# 5702359298 and 5702401684).
#
# GitHub reads this file for two things. It auto-requests the owner's review on
# a pull request touching a path below, unless the owner authored it. And
# `main-protect`'s `pull_request` rule carries `require_code_owner_review` (0009
# step 6, 2026-09-17), so such a pull request cannot merge without the owner's
# approving review on GitHub, which is how the owner approves a policy change.
#
# The owner is @tvofi and not the approver App: GitHub's docs list users and
# teams with explicit write access as code owners and name no App form. Every
# other path has no code owner, and the App's approving review serves those.
# docs/HANDOVER.md is deliberately absent: it carries state, not rules.
# Apps are never code owners — neither the approver nor the author App can
# satisfy an owner review; only @tvofi can (decision 0011).
#
# THE REQUIRED-CHECK ENFORCEMENT SURFACE (R6-D11-01, #1402). The tracked files
# that produce or implement the checks `main-protect-checks` requires carried no
# owner, so `require_code_owner_review` could not demand the owner for a change
# to the checks themselves. The surface is DERIVED, never carried: the
# `.github/workflows/*.yml`, the scripts their non-comment lines execute and
# what those import (#1515), the hooks, and their wiring. Re-derive it with
# `python3 tools/audit/round6/D11/fix/codeowners_gap.py`, which prints the
# surface size and how many of its files an owner-carrying pattern matches:
# against the pre-#1402 file that second count is zero, against this one it is
# the surface size. A new check script is covered only once it is owned below,
# or PINNED — restored from the base before every pull-request job that runs
# it (decision 0013; the harness prints which) — re-run the harness and extend
# this block when the surface moves. The governance instruments are pinned, so
# they carry no owner here: `.claude/workflows/*.mjs`, `gh_comment.py`,
# `vendor/`, `tools/audit/*.sh`, `record-predicate/` and `codeowners_gap.py`;
# so are the test-side graders the `tests/` block below names.
#
# Nothing in the test gate opens this file (tests/closure.py lists it INERT).

/CLAUDE.md                                @tvofi
/AGENTS.md                                @tvofi
/.claude/rules/                           @tvofi
/.cursor/rules/                           @tvofi
/.claude/skills/steward/SKILL.md          @tvofi
/.claude/workflows/web-fragments.md       @tvofi
/tools/audit/briefs/                      @tvofi
# COMMON.md is the finder's contract and is not policy (CLAUDE.md says so);
# a later line with a path and no owner un-owns it, because the last matching
# pattern wins.
/tools/audit/briefs/COMMON.md
/tools/audit/README.md                    @tvofi
/tools/audit/harnesses/README.md          @tvofi
/tests/README.md                          @tvofi
/docs/decisions/                          @tvofi
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md         @tvofi
/.github/CODEOWNERS                       @tvofi
# The ratchet caps (decision 0013, the owner's ruling of 2026-09-24: policy
# and budget files are the owner's). A budget may only move down without the
# owner, and CLAUDE.md rule 2 already asks the owner before a raise; owning the
# files makes GitHub enforce what that sentence asks. Named one by one, never
# `*_budgets.json`: a new cap file is owned when it is added here.
/.claude/workflows/policy_budgets.json    @tvofi
/tests/coverage_budgets.json              @tvofi
/tests/mutation_budgets.json              @tvofi
/tests/stress_budgets.json                @tvofi
/tests/structure_budgets.json             @tvofi
/tests/typing_budgets.json                @tvofi

# --- The required-check enforcement surface (R6-D11-01, #1402). ---
# The workflow files that hold the jobs whose status contexts the ruleset
# requires. The whole directory: every file here is a workflow on `main`.
/.github/workflows/                       @tvofi
# The hooks that run in every seat's session, and the wiring that gives a
# session its hooks. `always-fails.sh` is a deliberately unwired control; the
# whole directory is the surface.
/.claude/hooks/                           @tvofi
/.claude/settings.json                    @tvofi
# The governance scripts the required-check jobs execute, and what they
# import, carry no owner (decision 0013): every job a pull request reaches
# restores them from the base before it grades, so an edit cannot change the
# check that grades it -- `codeowners_gap.py --check` reads the restores.
# The wave scripts a required job EVALUATES by path: `check-wave-script.mjs`
# runs them, and `policy_lint.mjs` builds `web-fix-wave.js`'s VERDICT_RE with
# `new Function` inside the corpus lint (#1515 review, round 1). They are the
# graded artifacts, so no restore can pin them; they stay owned.
/.claude/workflows/audit-find.js          @tvofi
/.claude/workflows/audit-verify.js        @tvofi
/.claude/workflows/web-fix-wave.js        @tvofi
# The test scripts the gate's jobs execute directly -- by interpreter or by
# their own `./` path -- and the modules those import (#1515), where no pin can
# hold (decision 0013, amended 2026-09-24): the suite (`run.sh` and what `fast`
# and `browser` load) must run the pull request's code, and `closure.py` and
# `derive_closures.sh` carry the rosters a new test script or a newly read file
# edits in the same pull request, so a base copy would refuse that pull request.
# The single-job graders a job runs before any code of the pull request's
# (`mutation_table.py`, `typing_ruler.py`, `coverage_ratchet.py`,
# `delivery_status.py`, `nightly_status.py`) are PINNED and carry no owner; so
# are `nightly_ha.py` and `replay.py`, which no pull-request job runs.
/tests/card_browser.mjs                   @tvofi
/tests/closure.py                         @tvofi
/tests/derive_closures.sh                 @tvofi
/tests/env_drift.py                       @tvofi
/tests/golden.py                          @tvofi
/tests/harness.py                         @tvofi
/tests/plan_view.py                       @tvofi
/tests/profiles.py                        @tvofi
/tests/run.sh                             @tvofi
/tests/stress.py                          @tvofi
